## What it does
 
Most people have PDFs they need to extract information from — reports, research papers,
contracts, documentation. Instead of manually searching through pages, this tool lets
you upload any PDF and ask plain English questions about it. Answers include the exact
source excerpts used, so you can verify them.
 
---
 
## How it works
 
```
1. PDF uploaded      → text extracted page by page with PyMuPDF
2. Text chunked      → split into 500-char overlapping chunks via LangChain
3. Chunks embedded   → converted to vectors with sentence-transformers (all-MiniLM-L6-v2)
4. Vectors stored    → indexed locally with FAISS for fast similarity search
5. Question asked    → question embedded → top 3 matching chunks retrieved
6. Answer generated  → chunks + question sent to Groq API → answer streamed back
```
 
---
 
## Stack
 
| Layer      | Technology                                       |
|------------|--------------------------------------------------|
| Frontend   | HTML / CSS / JavaScript                          |
| Backend    | FastAPI, Python                                  |
| AI Model   | Groq API — llama-3.3-70b-versatile               |
| Embeddings | sentence-transformers (all-MiniLM-L6-v2)         |
| Vector DB  | FAISS (local)                                    |
| PDF Parse  | PyMuPDF                                          |
| Chunking   | LangChain RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter         |
 
